flang emits the standard F77 hidden-length ABI for CHARACTER dummy arguments:
one trailing size_t per char arg, appended after all explicit args. scipy's
cython_blas/cython_lapack wrappers declare and call the Fortran symbols without
those hidden lengths, which is harmless where a lax C ABI ignores extra
arguments but traps under wasm's strictly-typed call_indirect
(signature_mismatch:dgemm_). Regenerate the wrappers so the wasm signature
matches the flang reference BLAS/LAPACK. Every wrapped char arg is a CHARACTER*1
flag (ilaenv/xerbla are not wrapped, and LSAME ignores the length), so length 1
is always correct. Only the internal _fortran_<name> extern and its call change;
the public cdef wrapper signature is untouched, so cython_blas/cython_lapack
consumers (scikit-learn, ...) stay ABI-compatible.

--- a/scipy/linalg/_generate_pyx.py
+++ b/scipy/linalg/_generate_pyx.py
@@ -538,6 +538,18 @@
     if name in WRAPPED_FUNCS:
         pyx_call_args[0] = ''.join([arg_casts(c_argtypes[0]), '&', argnames[0]])
     pyx_call_args = ', '.join(pyx_call_args)
+    # WASIX: flang emits the standard F77 hidden-length ABI for CHARACTER args
+    # (one trailing size_t per char arg). These cython wrappers omit them, which
+    # is harmless where a lax C ABI ignores extra args but traps under wasm's
+    # strictly-typed call_indirect. Append them so the wasm signature matches the
+    # flang reference BLAS/LAPACK. Every wrapped char arg is a CHARACTER*1 flag
+    # (ilaenv/xerbla are not wrapped), so the length is always 1 and LSAME reads
+    # only the first character regardless. The public wrapper signature
+    # (pyx_input_args) is untouched, so consumers stay ABI-compatible.
+    n_charlen = c_argtypes.count('char')
+    if n_charlen:
+        c_proto += ''.join(f', size_t _charlen{i}' for i in range(n_charlen))
+        pyx_call_args += ', ' + ', '.join(['1'] * n_charlen)
     blas_macro, blas_name = get_blas_macro_and_name(name, accelerate, ilp64)
     return f"""
 cdef extern from "{header_name}":
@@ -692,6 +704,10 @@
